  "content": {
    "id": "p7-q13-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": null,
    "prompt": "Find the dimensions of a rectangle whose area is $3\\text{ m}^2$ and whose perimeter is $7\\text{ m}$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\frac32\\text{ m}$ by $2\\text{ m}$.",
      "worked": "Let the dimensions be $x$ metres and $y$ metres.\n$$\\begin{align*}2x+2y&=7\\\\y&=\\frac72-x\\\\x\\left(\\frac72-x\\right)&=3\\\\7x-2x^2&=6\\\\2x^2-7x+6&=0\\\\(2x-3)(x-2)&=0\\\\x&=\\frac32\\text{ or }2\\end{align*}$$\nThe corresponding other dimension is $2$ or $\\frac32$ metres. Thus the rectangle is $\\frac32\\text{ m}$ by $2\\text{ m}$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 88
  },
